# Scoped to the `zeek-image` Trivy job only (security-scan.yml passes this file
# via `trivyignores:`); the other Trivy jobs never read it.
#
# CVE-2026-110858, CVE-2026-42284, CVE-2026-78676 (all CRITICAL, python3-git
# 3.1.44-1, fixed in 3.1.44-1+deb13u1): GitPython command injection / code
# execution through attacker-controlled refspecs, clone options or git config.
# zeek/zeek:9.0.1 (sha256:524cb0ce...249dd0, pushed 2026-10-26, the newest tag on
# Docker Hub as of 2026-11-03) still ships python3-git 3.1.44-1, so no published
# pin clears them. python3-git is a dependency of zkg, the Zeek package manager.
# Not reachable as deployed: every capture path (host_capture.sh,
# stream_capture.sh, zeek_connect_host.sh, zeek_run_pcap.sh) runs the `zeek`
# binary only, never zkg or any Python, and no file in the repo calls zkg or
# GitPython (git grep, 2026-11-03). Tracked in #577 and in SOP-008's Tracked
# Exceptions table. The exp: date makes Trivy fail again on its own — bump the
# image or re-justify before then; do not just extend it.
#
# Retired 2026-11-03: CVE-2026-48930 (libnode115/nodejs). 9.0.1 ships the fixed
# 20.19.2+dfsg-1+deb13u3 (read from the image's dpkg status), so its exception
# is removed rather than extended.
CVE-2026-110858 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-42284 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-78676 exp:2026-11-30
